<!--
  =====================================================================
  stunt_system - LANGUAGE: English (reference + automatic fallback)
  =====================================================================
  HOW TO CREATE A NEW LANGUAGE (no script changes needed, works with .luac):
    1. Copy this file (lang/en.xml) to lang/<code>.xml
       (e.g. lang/es.xml, lang/ru.xml). Use the 2-letter ISO code.
    2. Change code="..." (shown on the header button of the Manager Alt+F2, e.g. ES)
       and name="..." (name shown in the footer on mouse hover, e.g. Español).
    3. Translate ONLY the TEXT between the tags. Do NOT change the id="...".
    4. Restart the resource (restart stunt_system). The language button shows up by
       itself in the top-left corner of the Manager (Alt+F2): PT | EN | ES ...
  RULES:
    - Any key missing from your file falls back to this en.xml automatically
      (the server console reports how many keys each language is missing).
    - {nome}, {valor}, {tempo}, {n}... are values filled in by the script: keep them
      in the text (you may move them inside the sentence). A "$" before them is the
      money symbol, e.g. ${valor} -> $5000.
    - #RRGGBB changes the text color in chat/HUD (e.g. #FF9900 = orange). Keep them.
    - In XML, write &lt; for "<", &gt; for ">" and &amp; for "&".
    - Spaces at the start/end of a text are ignored.
  The chosen language is saved on the player's PC (stunt_lang.xml) and shared with
  stunt_tools (when it is running on the server): changing it in one changes the other.
  SERVER chat messages are sent in each player's own language.
  =====================================================================
-->
